Dumpling season is officially back.

@luckydumplingmarket returns to Elder Park today, bringing some of the city’s best Asian eats, bars and live entertainment back to the banks of the Torrens. And this year, there’s even more time to get amongst it.

For the first time, Fridays are starting at 12pm, meaning lunch by the river is officially on the agenda. The market is also running across four weekends, with 27 food vendors, including six new faces, and OzAsia’s iconic moon lanterns lighting up the park. So whether it’s a Friday lunch, a balmy Saturday night or a Sunday afternoon with the family, we’ll see you by the river.

It’s the opening weekend of Lucky Dumpling Market and @ozasiafestival 2026, and here’s what’s happening for your entertainment – in addition to the menagerie of stunning OzAsia Festival moon lanterns around the market!

Onstage acts kick off just after 7pm this evening, and from 2pm Saturday and Sunday. Market gates are open and vendors are serving now, and from 12pm on Saturday and Sunday. 

A text version of the schedule is available at luckydumplingmarket.com - link in our stories. 

