Slowly, Stamford Hospital continues its journey in global readership. The days of my publicists pitching have ended. They kicked off my career (🙏). Festival organizers hearing about this book through word-of-mouth are trusting in it, and for that they have my gratitude.

I believe in the power of story to change the course of someone’s life—which is why I have a lifetime goal of a million copies of Stamford Hospital being in hands. It’s not about the money (royalties are puny); it’s about how reading this story could remind anyone that they have their own to tell. Even when life seems to have come to so little. 

@byronwritersfestival and @jessica__alice__ this reel’s a love note for you for believing in my book, a year after publication. We’re on a path of a lifetime together.

