Getting ready to start glazing tomorrow. I’ve been racing against time to get everything ready for the upcoming North Coast Mud Trail. It’s hard to believe it’s only days away - Saturday and Sunday 22nd and 23rd March.
Our Gittoes Lane, Possum Creek has been graded just in time. 
We are Studio 8. Follow the signs.
This year, we are back to displaying everything on tables along the veranda under cover. There will be so many goodies available, including homemade organic Mullum plum jam and Seville orange marmalade made from our own fruit.
My memoir Merging with Nature will be available at a special price. It tells of a life of campaigning globally for baby seals, whales, pink dolphins in the Amazon, kangaroos and includes meetings with amazing people, like Prince Philip, the Dalai Lama and Spike Milligan. It includes my involvement in founding Greenpeace Australia and other organisations.
This year too will include beautiful artworks by my wife Jo, granddaughter Bodhi and partner Corey and good friend Annie Peros.
Some of these plates will be available on the weekend, others are commissions.
